WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.879
All of us who learn languages, and myself
included, we eventually want to speak. We

00:00:05.879 --> 00:00:11.370
want to output. Even though LingQ
emphasizes input and recognizes the

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.870
importance of input in making our brain
familiar with the language, the words, the

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:20.820
phrases, the pronunciation, eventually we
want to output. A good place to

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.660
start is writing, because there's no
pressure. You can look things up. You can

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.279
look up the correct ending, you know, the
correct tense to use or other

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:34.200
grammatical points. You can check the
word in your vocabulary section, or you

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.879
can save a bunch of words, let's say that
you've tagged, and then try to use these

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:43.590
words in your writing. And other members
of our community can correct these for

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:48.660
you in the Exchange. And then you can
import this as learning material. So, for

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:54.840
those of you who are prepared to
practice writing, make it a habit to

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.969
write a little bit, because it's a good
way to start yourself towards being a

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:04.489
more comfortable speaker of the language.

